Experience levels aren't only skill slots.  They increase your
chances to hit, and reduce spell failure rates.  Having cure
sickness at 0% failure can be very useful in certain conditions,
and for a Valk or a Sam, it requires a fair number of XL.
Samurai can also use attack spells fairly effectively, which
means ranged attacks without having to switch weapons.

> And anoter point generally is; why unnecessarily increase XL
> when you will have negative effects with tougher monsters
> appearing. (This is not so relevant in the OP's case, though,
> since he's already at the Sanctum.)

I tend to eat all the Wraiths I can in the Valley of the Dead,
for the added hit points and added spell casting abilities.
I've not noticed any real negative effects; by that time, there
really aren't any normally generated monsters you have to be
afraid of.

